From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 19:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] base: stop shipping a made-up compositor geometry

The generic base layer declared 1920x1080+0+0r0s1, which is a webOS TV
resolution and describes no phone we support. It is what every machine
without a per-machine file underneath it received.

It is also redundant: surface-manager.sh already falls back to exactly
the same string when configd has no compositorGeometry -

    export WEBOS_COMPOSITOR_GEOMETRY=$(luna-send ... || echo "1920x1080+0+0r0s1")

- so removing it here changes the value on no device at all. What it
changes is that a guess stops being presented as data. It had already
been read as data once: 50-luna-platform used to take DPI from the
shipped luna-platform.conf as a fallback, and that invented number
became the effective DPI of every device without an adaptation.

On Halium machines luneos-device-config derives the real geometry from
the DRM connector and feeds it in through the configd overlay layer,
which outranks this one, so those devices never saw this value anyway.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
+++ b/configs/layers/base/com.webos.surfacemanager.json	2026-08-24 19:31:30.387541411 +0200
@@ -1,3 +1,2 @@
 {
-    "compositorGeometry": "1920x1080+0+0r0s1"
 }
